WEBVTT

01:42.519 --> 01:44.062
‎From what you've told me,

01:44.145 --> 01:47.398
‎I can't rule out the possibility that
‎he's experiencing cyberpsychosis.

01:47.482 --> 01:49.567
‎I need more information.

01:49.651 --> 01:51.486
‎Can you describe
‎his behavior in more detail?

01:51.569 --> 01:55.073
‎What symptoms
‎should I keep an eye out for?

01:55.156 --> 01:59.077
‎Has he ever acted... not himself?
‎Even temporarily.

02:00.787 --> 02:03.998
‎There was this one time
‎he got pretty weird...

02:04.082 --> 02:07.377
‎Aha! Was he more... girlish?

02:07.460 --> 02:10.380
‎Girlish? I dunno?

02:10.463 --> 02:12.924
‎Was actin' real strange, is all.

02:13.007 --> 02:15.885
‎And this only happened once?

02:15.969 --> 02:16.970
‎I think...

02:17.554 --> 02:21.015
‎Can cyberpsychosis flip
‎your whole personality?

02:21.099 --> 02:23.184
‎Not necessarily, no.

02:23.268 --> 02:25.603
‎How about hearing voices
‎that aren't there?

02:25.687 --> 02:28.731
‎You mean like an imaginary friend?

02:29.315 --> 02:31.276
‎Uh... I'm just spitballin'.

02:31.359 --> 02:33.820
‎-Are you sure?
‎-Yeah.

02:33.903 --> 02:35.530
‎Appreciate the info.

02:35.613 --> 02:37.824
‎Can I ping ya back
‎if I notice anything else?

02:37.907 --> 02:39.117
‎Of course.

02:39.200 --> 02:41.119
‎Thanks... Talk to ya later.

02:44.080 --> 02:48.251
‎So Capri hasn't overwritten her host...
‎but they talk to each other?

02:48.334 --> 02:51.004
‎Maybe the overwrite is still in progress.

02:52.380 --> 02:55.508
‎Which would mean... Agh, I don't know!

02:57.218 --> 02:59.637
‎There's too many unknown variables.

02:59.721 --> 03:02.640
‎Why'd you run away? Capri...

03:04.100 --> 03:05.143
‎Initiate test.

03:20.992 --> 03:23.411
‎Capri, enough. Stop clownin' around.

03:24.245 --> 03:25.955
‎Honestly...

03:26.039 --> 03:27.165
‎Most impressive.

03:27.999 --> 03:32.211
‎She can hack or destroy
‎any electronic system in an instant.

03:32.754 --> 03:36.424
‎This will revolutionize
‎how we conduct warfare.

03:36.507 --> 03:39.052
‎Well, there are still a few bugs.

03:41.262 --> 03:44.015
‎Ah, shit. Yank the chip.

03:44.098 --> 03:45.767
‎-On it.
‎-What just happened?

03:46.351 --> 03:51.022
‎On average, only about 7% of test subjects
‎survive Capricorn's installation.

03:51.606 --> 03:57.028
‎About half die within 12 hours.
‎And none have ever lived beyond the 48.

03:57.111 --> 03:59.948
‎That's completely unsustainable.

04:00.031 --> 04:01.908
‎It boils down to compatibility.

04:01.991 --> 04:03.451
‎We'll find a compatible host,

04:03.534 --> 04:05.745
‎and that will help us
‎in finding a permanent solution.

04:06.246 --> 04:09.499
‎This thing, this fusion
‎of digital constructs...

04:09.582 --> 04:11.251
‎What if it escapes into cyberspace?

04:11.751 --> 04:14.963
‎Precisely why it requires
‎a human host in the first place.

04:15.046 --> 04:19.384
‎The fragility of organic matter
‎serves as the perfect safeguard.

04:19.467 --> 04:22.637
‎Worst case, we can implant the host body

04:22.720 --> 04:24.973
‎with explosives
‎or toxins as a kill switch.

04:25.598 --> 04:31.980
‎This way, we also eliminate the threat
‎of her escaping across the Blackwall.

04:33.564 --> 04:36.276
‎So the body serves as her prison.

04:41.322 --> 04:43.324
‎-Next test subject.
‎-Yes, ma'am.

04:44.826 --> 04:48.079
‎Since Tanaka's death,
‎it's like Counterintel's gone dark.

04:48.830 --> 04:50.873
‎Our patience is wearing thin.

04:51.416 --> 04:53.209
‎How many subjects dead?

04:54.210 --> 04:55.586
‎We'll never find a host.

04:55.670 --> 04:57.880
‎Additional funding is out of the question.

05:01.050 --> 05:02.885
‎It's all right, Capri.

05:04.220 --> 05:05.972
‎Ma'am, this is going too far!

05:06.055 --> 05:07.890
‎They won't take you away from me.

05:12.020 --> 05:13.396
‎No! Stop the test!

05:21.070 --> 05:23.156
‎Return fire! Power weapons only!

05:23.239 --> 05:25.533
‎-Fuck! Agh! My face!
‎-Smart guns won't work!

05:25.616 --> 05:28.745
‎This was a waste of time.
‎A disappointment.

05:29.370 --> 05:31.247
‎But Capri is almost complete!

05:31.331 --> 05:33.666
‎She's perfect!
‎Just missing the right host!

05:34.459 --> 05:35.793
‎It's over.

05:35.877 --> 05:39.172
‎Project Capricorn is hereby terminated.

05:39.255 --> 05:41.883
‎Capri? Don't you fuckin' touch her!

05:41.966 --> 05:46.471
‎Capri!

05:49.390 --> 05:50.683
‎Morning already.

05:50.767 --> 05:53.644
‎You oughta scamper on back.

05:58.274 --> 06:00.401
‎Really am the only one who can see you.

06:00.485 --> 06:04.155
‎I ain't a hallucination!
‎How many times do I gotta explain it!

06:04.238 --> 06:06.949
‎Yeah, yeah, digital construct, I get it...

06:07.533 --> 06:09.702
‎Just stop eavesdroppin'
‎on my thoughts, will ya?

06:09.786 --> 06:12.705
‎Pretty big ask considerin'
‎we share the same brain.

06:12.789 --> 06:14.415
‎Whatever...

06:14.499 --> 06:19.629
‎You haven't even thanked me for fixin'
‎your brain and gettin' ya on your feet.

06:19.712 --> 06:21.339
‎Saved your life, don't ya know!

06:21.422 --> 06:24.550
‎So? My body's the only thing
‎keepin' you alive, too.

06:24.634 --> 06:27.762
‎Details! What's wrong
‎with a lil give-and-take?

06:28.346 --> 06:30.473
‎Fact is... you did get me outta that bed.

06:30.556 --> 06:33.476
‎Got me past hospital security.

06:34.060 --> 06:36.354
‎I believe you... I guess.

06:37.855 --> 06:39.232
‎Sheesh, you're so weird.

06:39.941 --> 06:43.402
‎-Weird?
‎-Your body's failing on every level.

06:43.486 --> 06:46.072
‎Thought you'd be all,
‎"Yay, I can walk again!"

06:46.155 --> 06:47.657
‎You're almost all healthy now!

06:48.157 --> 06:49.242
‎I ‎am‎ happy...

06:50.326 --> 06:52.578
‎But... it's not enough.

06:52.662 --> 06:54.747
‎Listen, I can't make you fly
‎or anything like that.

06:54.831 --> 06:57.250
‎So don't go gettin' greedy.

06:58.334 --> 07:00.628
‎At least... not unless we get
‎the chip back, right?

07:00.711 --> 07:04.632
‎Yup. Half my programming
‎is still lodged inside him.

07:04.715 --> 07:08.261
‎And if I have all of you,
‎you can fix me completely?

07:08.344 --> 07:10.555
‎Oh no, way beyond that.

07:10.638 --> 07:13.391
‎Beyond that? Can't even imagine it.

07:13.474 --> 07:14.517
‎Yeah?

07:14.600 --> 07:19.397
‎Because that was...
‎the best my body could ever do.

07:21.399 --> 07:24.569
‎I can take you back
‎to how you were. Promise!

07:38.833 --> 07:41.252
‎You're still Capri, right?

07:42.628 --> 07:43.629
‎Right?

07:45.506 --> 07:46.507
‎Capri...

07:55.600 --> 07:57.477
‎Oh, are we rolling?

07:57.560 --> 08:00.271
‎Hey NC, we're comin' to ya live today!

08:00.354 --> 08:02.773
‎Let's go! Kick it off, D!

08:03.441 --> 08:06.527
‎To the butchers responsible
‎for torching my clan.

08:06.611 --> 08:10.281
‎I've been tellin' you to step up,
‎but you've given me nothing.

08:10.364 --> 08:13.201
‎The next target shows how serious I am.

08:13.284 --> 08:14.785
‎Jake Collins.

08:14.869 --> 08:17.413
‎Deputy Chief
‎of Arasaka Counterintelligence.

08:17.497 --> 08:19.290
‎He's gettin' hit as I speak.

08:24.504 --> 08:26.255
‎Yo! He ran off that way!

08:26.339 --> 08:29.550
‎Hey! Come on out!

08:29.634 --> 08:30.885
‎Got one!

08:32.803 --> 08:35.932
‎Roman, that's a killer angle!
‎Helluva money shot!

08:42.271 --> 08:43.689
‎My arm...

08:44.273 --> 08:45.441
‎Someone find it...

08:45.525 --> 08:46.901
‎-Someone find my arm...
‎-Yo.

08:46.984 --> 08:49.987
‎Ah! I don't know anything... Nothing!

08:50.071 --> 08:53.449
‎Bullshit. Why would Counterintel
‎be kept out of the loop?

08:53.533 --> 08:55.201
‎I'm telling the truth!

08:55.284 --> 08:57.161
‎Nothing about a nomad camp--

08:57.745 --> 09:01.707
‎Then give me some names!
‎Who the fuck knows? Tell me!

09:01.791 --> 09:05.336
‎I don't know any names.
‎They just transferred here recently!

09:05.419 --> 09:08.673
‎I don't know anything.
‎Please... I need help.

09:08.756 --> 09:10.508
‎Please...

09:10.591 --> 09:14.178
‎-Let's delta. D! Gotta go!
‎-What?

09:20.142 --> 09:22.103
‎-My arm...
‎-Last call for loot!

09:22.186 --> 09:24.438
‎What? Already?

09:33.614 --> 09:36.784
‎Man, D's a machine.
‎Could wipe 'Saka by hisself.

09:36.867 --> 09:41.455
‎Right! Like, what's stoppin' us
‎from hittin' 'em dead on!

09:45.835 --> 09:47.461
‎Don't throw your shit, choomie.

09:47.545 --> 09:48.754
‎Mega rude.

09:48.838 --> 09:52.466
‎How have I not learned
‎a single goddamn thing? Fuck!

10:18.826 --> 10:21.996
‎-Huh? Who's this bitch?
‎-What do I do?

10:22.913 --> 10:23.914
‎Run her over.

10:23.998 --> 10:25.875
‎No. She's a friend.

10:27.460 --> 10:30.046
‎-How'd she find us?
‎-I pinged her.

10:32.340 --> 10:33.507
‎Did you watch?

10:34.383 --> 10:36.218
‎-I did.
‎-And?

10:36.302 --> 10:39.513
‎This mean you're ready to join the fight?
‎Is that why you're here, Omi?

10:40.264 --> 10:43.017
‎What you're doing is completely unhinged.

10:43.100 --> 10:44.393
‎So you liked it?

10:44.477 --> 10:45.936
‎Is that what you think?

10:46.812 --> 10:47.813
‎It scared me.

10:47.897 --> 10:50.941
‎It's not like you don't know
‎where this road leads, right?

10:51.025 --> 10:53.319
‎Course I do. Doesn't matter.

10:53.402 --> 10:57.156
‎What you're doing now...
‎it's the same shit those corpos did to us.

10:58.240 --> 10:59.575
‎The same?

10:59.659 --> 11:02.953
‎This senseless violence... it isn't you.

11:03.037 --> 11:04.288
‎Not the old you.

11:05.039 --> 11:07.583
‎Is there even a point to all this?

11:07.667 --> 11:09.627
‎You know what it is.

11:09.710 --> 11:11.796
‎-Revenge?
‎-Yeah.

11:11.879 --> 11:15.841
‎It's insanity. You've gone too far.
‎Innocent folks are gettin' caught in it!

11:15.925 --> 11:17.843
‎They're all 'Saka!

11:17.927 --> 11:19.887
‎I'm just tryna smoke out
‎the ones still hiding!

11:19.970 --> 11:23.349
‎So what, you're gonna flatline everyone
‎at Arasaka just because?

11:23.432 --> 11:25.601
‎Why the fuck did you even come here?

11:25.684 --> 11:27.853
‎To rag on me? Go home!

11:27.937 --> 11:30.231
‎No! I came to stop you!

11:32.316 --> 11:34.068
‎The fuck?

11:34.151 --> 11:36.821
‎What the hell are you doin'?

11:36.904 --> 11:39.198
‎Giving you a taste of your own medicine!

11:43.702 --> 11:45.162
‎Damn it!

11:54.630 --> 11:56.882
‎Fuck you, Omi.

11:57.508 --> 12:01.762
‎What the hell am I supposed to do? Huh?

12:03.973 --> 12:05.141
‎The fuck do I do?

12:05.891 --> 12:07.393
‎Tell me!

12:07.476 --> 12:09.979
‎Stop it, D! You gotta chill!

12:10.062 --> 12:11.772
‎-Outta the way, Roman.
‎-I'm not movin'!

12:11.856 --> 12:13.858
‎-You--
‎-Your gonk revenge plan's not working!

12:13.941 --> 12:15.401
‎Time to give it up!

12:15.484 --> 12:17.153
‎Where'd that come from?

12:17.236 --> 12:21.282
‎She's right. Haven't been yourself.
‎The D I know--

12:21.365 --> 12:22.533
‎Just shut up!

12:23.117 --> 12:25.035
‎The D you know? Fuck you.

12:25.119 --> 12:26.537
‎You two don't know shit!

12:35.546 --> 12:36.547
‎Fuck!

12:46.557 --> 12:47.558
‎Um...

12:47.641 --> 12:50.811
‎So you were in the same clan as D?

12:54.523 --> 12:55.774
‎And you are?

12:57.985 --> 12:59.528
‎Can't say I approve.

13:01.030 --> 13:04.533
‎That is, a kid your age
‎taggin' along with him.

13:04.617 --> 13:06.452
‎It doesn't sit well with me at all.

13:07.244 --> 13:09.288
‎Why not walk away?

13:09.371 --> 13:12.458
‎You seem fed up
‎with how he's been acting.

13:13.834 --> 13:17.963
‎-I saw him laughing a little while ago.
‎-Laughing?

13:18.047 --> 13:20.883
‎The first time D tapped into that power...

13:20.966 --> 13:24.261
‎He just looked so happy.
‎Was like he couldn't stop laughin'.

13:25.429 --> 13:27.973
‎Like everything changed.
‎He seemed so different.

13:28.724 --> 13:30.684
‎And I thought...

13:30.768 --> 13:34.104
‎"Oh, so ‎that's‎ how this guy laughs."

13:34.188 --> 13:36.357
‎Made me wonder if that was the real D.

13:36.982 --> 13:41.737
‎Made me wanna catch
‎that side of D on film again.

13:44.114 --> 13:45.115
‎Yeah. I understand.

13:45.908 --> 13:48.285
‎He... He's got a really good smile.

13:48.869 --> 13:50.246
‎Here's your order.

13:51.664 --> 13:53.874
‎So, you haven't seen him in a while?

13:54.416 --> 13:56.502
‎No. Not since you know what.

13:57.294 --> 14:01.006
‎Um... Can I ask what happened?

14:02.174 --> 14:06.303
‎First, you mind turnin' that thing off?
‎I don't much like being on camera.

14:06.387 --> 14:08.264
‎Sorry. Habit.

14:09.139 --> 14:10.766
‎So what has he told you?

14:10.849 --> 14:12.601
‎Bits and pieces...

14:12.685 --> 14:15.771
‎-Never goes into detail.
‎-Yeah.

14:18.023 --> 14:20.276
‎He was all smiles on that day, too.

14:21.068 --> 14:24.280
‎We stole some random jalopy from a motel.

14:25.155 --> 14:27.658
‎On the way home,
‎he was cacklin' like a coyote.

14:28.450 --> 14:30.494
‎Being his usual goofy self.

14:31.787 --> 14:35.541
‎He was still laughin'
‎when we saw the smoke.

14:36.417 --> 14:40.170
‎In the desert,
‎you can see smoke from miles out.

14:41.171 --> 14:43.924
‎We could tell it was comin' from camp.

14:44.633 --> 14:48.053
‎We weren't laughin' anymore.
‎We went real quiet, then.

14:50.139 --> 14:53.559
‎The rest is kind of a blur.
‎That was the last time I saw him.

14:54.602 --> 14:58.564
‎Not once did the fool ever contact me.
‎For all I knew, he was buzzard bait.

14:59.148 --> 15:01.692
‎I had my own troubles to deal with, so...

15:02.192 --> 15:04.820
‎-Um... Not sure I should ask.
‎-Ask what?

15:05.571 --> 15:07.072
‎Were you guys like... romantic?

15:11.160 --> 15:15.289
‎Was that your takeaway back there?
‎A spat between lovebirds?

15:16.749 --> 15:19.460
‎Well, uh... they say love comes
‎in all shapes and sizes...

15:21.962 --> 15:25.424
‎That's too good!
‎Now I see why David likes you.

15:25.507 --> 15:27.134
‎Huh? David?

15:27.217 --> 15:29.386
‎What, he never told you his name?

15:30.137 --> 15:32.765
‎Oh, that's right,
‎goes by D these days, doesn't he?

15:33.766 --> 15:36.477
‎Gonna start calling him
‎by his first name now?

15:37.186 --> 15:38.395
‎I could, but...

15:39.355 --> 15:43.150
‎No. Only ever known him as D.
‎That's who he is.

15:43.776 --> 15:44.777
‎Sure.

16:07.049 --> 16:10.803
‎Avida? If you're looking
‎for Kiril, he's out right now.

16:11.303 --> 16:13.889
‎Just here to drop somethin' off
‎for him anyway.

16:19.520 --> 16:20.980
‎Just slot this shard into his terminal.

16:21.063 --> 16:22.815
‎It'll pull the files
‎we need automatically.

16:23.524 --> 16:27.778
‎Got it from one of my old contacts.
‎Should still work.

16:31.615 --> 16:32.616
‎Got it!

16:35.077 --> 16:36.453
‎Avida?

16:37.121 --> 16:38.455
‎What brings you here?

16:39.164 --> 16:42.960
‎I came to see you...
‎They let me wait inside.

16:43.544 --> 16:45.546
‎You could've called first.

16:46.296 --> 16:47.965
‎What was so urgent?

16:48.632 --> 16:51.051
‎Are you familiar with Soulkiller?

16:51.635 --> 16:56.265
‎Soulkiller? Of course I'm familiar.
‎But where is this coming from?

16:56.348 --> 17:00.060
‎Well, I thought that technology
‎could maybe save Talia.

17:00.144 --> 17:02.646
‎If her body's failing,
‎why not find her a new one?

17:02.730 --> 17:03.731
‎Impossible.

17:04.356 --> 17:06.400
‎Even if we managed
‎to create her construct,

17:06.483 --> 17:08.861
‎body transferal technology doesn't exist.

17:08.944 --> 17:10.571
‎But there's potential!

17:10.654 --> 17:12.031
‎No, there isn't.

17:12.114 --> 17:16.660
‎Besides which, Soulkiller
‎was proprietary to Arasaka.

17:16.744 --> 17:18.495
‎It's not a program they'll let anyone use.

17:19.371 --> 17:21.498
‎But... doesn't Kang Tao
‎have its own version?

17:22.750 --> 17:23.876
‎Where did you hear that?

17:23.959 --> 17:27.421
‎I didn't, just assumed.
‎And that sounded like a "yes."

17:27.504 --> 17:28.839
‎No, we don't.

17:28.922 --> 17:30.049
‎Are you sure?

17:30.132 --> 17:31.759
‎It's impossible.

17:31.842 --> 17:34.219
‎Arasaka already cut
‎their commercial investment for it.

17:34.845 --> 17:37.139
‎-Really?
‎-Yes.

17:38.140 --> 17:39.600
‎You came all this way to ask that?

17:39.683 --> 17:41.351
‎So what if I did?

17:41.435 --> 17:44.104
‎If this could save Talia's life,
‎shouldn't I?

17:44.188 --> 17:45.189
‎You need to stay calm.

17:46.023 --> 17:49.526
‎You're starting to sound like Talia
‎with this cyber-fetishization talk.

17:50.110 --> 17:52.905
‎Miracle cures, pseudoscience,
‎these things won't help.

17:53.739 --> 17:55.532
‎We must remain grounded.

17:56.200 --> 17:57.534
‎You mean, like you?

17:57.618 --> 17:58.952
‎That's right.

17:59.495 --> 18:01.330
‎No... You're right.

18:02.081 --> 18:05.250
‎Shouldn't have barged in on you like this.

18:05.334 --> 18:07.669
‎I know you've been under
‎a lot of pressure.

18:07.753 --> 18:11.048
‎-Go on home, get some rest.
‎-Yeah.

18:15.552 --> 18:16.553
‎Avida?

18:18.388 --> 18:21.016
‎You're not the only one
‎who wants to help Talia.

18:22.351 --> 18:23.560
‎I hope you understand that.

18:25.729 --> 18:26.730
‎I do.

19:02.432 --> 19:03.851
‎Talia?

19:20.951 --> 19:22.119
‎Nova!

19:35.215 --> 19:36.800
‎Soooo preem!

19:36.884 --> 19:39.136
‎Can't believe the projector still works!

19:39.219 --> 19:40.220
‎You like it?

19:40.304 --> 19:43.599
‎Course I do!
‎Always dreamed of watchin' a movie here!

19:43.682 --> 19:44.892
‎Thought so.

19:44.975 --> 19:46.810
‎Too bad this movie's a total stinker.

19:47.603 --> 19:48.896
‎Bushido X‎ is showin' too.

19:49.396 --> 19:50.856
‎Nah, this one's fine.

19:52.399 --> 19:53.859
‎Ah, before I forget.

19:53.942 --> 19:55.485
‎Take your pick.

19:56.153 --> 19:59.198
‎You have two cams?
‎I call dibs on the little one.

20:00.699 --> 20:04.286
‎-Ooh, it's working!
‎-Hey, listen...

20:04.369 --> 20:06.246
‎What? Oh, the hospital?

20:06.330 --> 20:07.998
‎I snuck out!

20:11.335 --> 20:13.712
‎Come on...

20:13.795 --> 20:16.006
‎Aw, were you worried for me?

20:16.089 --> 20:17.758
‎Course I was!

20:17.841 --> 20:21.720
‎Glad you're doin' okay, but come on...

20:22.846 --> 20:26.892
‎Won't lie, it wasn't great.
‎Couldn't walk 'til the other day.

20:27.976 --> 20:29.645
‎Right? Can you believe it?

20:32.814 --> 20:36.652
‎Sis, your survival stats are insane.
‎For real, for real.

20:37.527 --> 20:42.199
‎Teach me! I wanna be a strong,
‎independent woman like you!

20:42.741 --> 20:44.701
‎What was that, you weirdo!

20:49.456 --> 20:52.584
‎Hey! Been meanin'
‎to apologize to you, Talia!

20:52.668 --> 20:53.669
‎To me?

20:54.586 --> 20:55.963
‎You wound up in the hospital

20:56.046 --> 20:58.966
‎-'‎cause of D's chip, right?
‎-‎Ah...

20:59.049 --> 21:00.884
‎I'm really, really sorry.

21:00.968 --> 21:03.095
‎Why are you apologizing?

21:03.178 --> 21:05.055
‎It's not like you did it.

21:05.138 --> 21:06.932
‎I know, but... still...

21:07.516 --> 21:10.435
‎To tell ya the truth,
‎wasn't doin' so hot anyway.

21:10.519 --> 21:13.480
‎Kinda worked out in the end, huh?

21:13.563 --> 21:14.690
‎What?

21:16.775 --> 21:20.320
‎If we're gettin' things off our chest,
‎suppose I should apologize to you too.

21:20.404 --> 21:21.446
‎To me?

21:21.530 --> 21:25.450
‎'Cause of me you had
‎to put up with that old geezer.

21:25.534 --> 21:28.912
‎Always are gettin' me
‎in trouble. Even today.

21:30.330 --> 21:32.457
‎You're a good guy, Roman.

21:33.333 --> 21:34.960
‎I dunno 'bout that...

21:36.295 --> 21:39.965
‎Bastard thought he was so funny,
‎tellin' me I don't know love.

21:40.549 --> 21:44.136
‎What a jerk.
‎Can't he tell I'm too sick to date?

21:44.219 --> 21:46.263
‎Just stop to think for two millisecs.

21:46.346 --> 21:50.100
‎-Yeah... Didn't seem like he bought it.
‎-What's that?

21:50.183 --> 21:54.563
‎That I could be your boyfriend.
‎Idea of it had him crackin' up.

21:54.646 --> 21:56.898
‎Dunno why. I like you.

21:58.650 --> 22:00.652
‎Your film.

22:00.736 --> 22:02.487
‎Oh...

22:02.571 --> 22:05.365
‎But you like me, don't you?

22:06.908 --> 22:08.118
‎Uh... I mean...

22:09.619 --> 22:10.704
‎Don't you?

22:12.122 --> 22:15.751
‎Even if you don't,
‎still hope you're willin' to help me.

22:15.834 --> 22:17.210
‎Well, 'course...

22:19.588 --> 22:20.672
‎Can you take me to D?

22:21.214 --> 22:22.716
‎Why the heck would you want that?

22:22.799 --> 22:23.884
‎Can't help?

22:23.967 --> 22:25.761
‎I can, but...

22:25.844 --> 22:28.722
‎But what? Those vids all over the city...

22:29.389 --> 22:30.432
‎That's him, isn't it?

22:31.183 --> 22:33.769
‎And you're his cameraman? Right?

22:33.852 --> 22:35.479
‎Yeah, but...

22:35.562 --> 22:38.190
‎There some reason we shouldn't meet?

22:38.273 --> 22:39.524
‎Why would you want to?

22:40.275 --> 22:42.986
‎I mean, was 'cause of him
‎you landed in the hospital!

22:43.862 --> 22:44.988
‎That's...

22:47.699 --> 22:48.742
‎Why?

22:49.326 --> 22:52.370
‎-Talia?
‎-Sorry, gotta bounce.

22:52.454 --> 22:54.331
‎Wha... now? What about D?

22:55.207 --> 22:58.251
‎Let's hit pause. I'll buzz ya back.

22:58.335 --> 23:00.045
‎Gotta meet up with a choom.

23:01.797 --> 23:04.007
‎Your cam. Can I borrow it?

23:04.091 --> 23:05.383
‎Uh, sure, yeah.

23:06.343 --> 23:07.636
‎See ya 'round.

23:13.225 --> 23:15.727
‎Why'd you stop me? What about the chip?

23:15.811 --> 23:19.147
‎That lil cupcake would go
‎to hell and back for you, you know.

23:19.231 --> 23:22.275
‎Might even yank the chip out for you.

23:22.359 --> 23:24.569
‎Then lemme lay out the situation for him--

23:24.653 --> 23:26.780
‎You think that baby
‎would walk away unharmed?

23:28.657 --> 23:29.991
‎And think of the chip.

23:30.075 --> 23:32.828
‎If it winds up lost or falls
‎in someone else's pocket,

23:32.911 --> 23:35.205
‎our plan gets flushed down the crapper.

23:35.288 --> 23:37.165
‎Like if some corpo gets hold of it

23:37.249 --> 23:39.292
‎-and cracks it open?
‎-Ding-ding!

23:39.376 --> 23:43.922
‎Depending on what they find, there's
‎no telling what happens to either of us.

23:44.005 --> 23:46.675
‎It's not the safest option...

23:46.758 --> 23:51.429
‎but the fact that D has the chip
‎is a major opportunity.

23:51.513 --> 23:53.974
‎We need to play this carefully.

23:54.057 --> 23:56.434
‎He has a bad habit of rushing into things.

23:57.602 --> 24:01.690
‎Still can't believe Kang Tao
‎has a Soulkiller all its own.

24:02.274 --> 24:05.819
‎Got it through a backdoor deal
‎within Arasaka.

24:06.570 --> 24:08.446
‎Almost no one knows.

24:09.614 --> 24:11.491
‎Doesn't matter. Take a look here.

24:14.953 --> 24:15.954
‎What are they?

24:16.037 --> 24:18.081
‎Cryopreserved bodies, all of 'em.

24:18.665 --> 24:22.335
‎Stockpiled as would-be hosts
‎for minds extracted by Soulkiller.

24:22.419 --> 24:24.462
‎-Then...
‎-That's right.

24:24.546 --> 24:26.339
‎Kang Tao has all the tools we need.

24:26.423 --> 24:29.551
‎It's just the process itself
‎of mergin' mind with body

24:29.634 --> 24:31.386
‎that's still experimental.

24:31.469 --> 24:33.638
‎Avida, really sure about this?

24:33.722 --> 24:35.640
‎Practically an act of war
‎against your husband.

24:36.183 --> 24:39.102
‎I know. I've made my choice.

24:39.186 --> 24:43.148
‎You'll have to leave, flee the city,
‎unless you back outta this now.

24:43.773 --> 24:45.609
‎A little late for that.

24:46.484 --> 24:48.528
‎Besides, we're runnin' outta time.

24:48.612 --> 24:51.865
‎Soulkiller's bein' relocated
‎to a new facility. It's now or never.

24:53.909 --> 24:56.328
‎We can't take Talia in her condition...

24:56.411 --> 24:58.371
‎We'll do it ourselves.

24:58.955 --> 25:02.792
‎Copy Soulkiller. Grab a body for her.

25:05.045 --> 25:06.463
‎You're right.

25:08.882 --> 25:10.133
‎Let's run it.

26:49.941 --> 26:54.946
‎Subtitle translation by:
‎CD PROJEKT RED & Megumi Hunter
